  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Relay Local/Remote Authority Boundary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Status",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Draft.** Derived from Intake's [Hosted/Local Boundary](https://github.com/juliantorr-es/Intake/blob/main/docs/architecture/hosted-local-boundary.md) and adapted for Rig Relay's telemetry and alpha-sharing model.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Doctrine",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig Relay follows a split-brain architecture for all remote communication:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **Local Rig Relay Cockpit** is the authority. It holds raw artifacts, receipts, private code context, and protected action authority. It connects **outbound only** to any remote service. - **Remote Telemetry Store** (future) is a boring, append-only, content-light store. It receives ciphertext, redacted metadata, hashes, counts, and opaque artifact references. It has **no mutation authority**. - **External Agents** (future ACP/MCP) propose work. They do not own authority.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Canonical Redaction Boundary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The shared redaction module in `rig_relay.evidence.redaction` is the canonical implementation for content-light remote/shareable artifacts.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Local cockpit retains raw receipts, prompts, outputs, and source context. - Remote/shareable outputs are redacted or hashed before publication. - Remote data cannot authorize mutations, even if it is structurally valid. - Bundle builders, audit writers, and export helpers must route through the shared redaction boundary rather than copy their own sensitive-field rules.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Core Boundaries",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "No private keys in the remote store",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The remote telemetry store never holds private decryption keys. The local cockpit owns all decryption authority.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Local-only decryption",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sensitive data (raw receipts, prompts, model outputs, source context) is only decrypted within the local cockpit. The remote store sees only: - Content-light projections (counts, statuses, hashes) - Ciphertext of sensitive payloads (if encryption is enabled) - Redacted metadata (timestamps, event names, operation IDs)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Outbound-only sync",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The local cockpit initiates all connections to the remote store. The remote store never connects inbound to a local machine.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-17",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "No raw content in remote storage",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-18",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Data",
        "Local",
        "Remote"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Raw receipts",
          "✅ Full",
          "❌ Never"
        ],
        [
          "Raw prompts/outputs",
          "✅ Full",
          "❌ Never"
        ],
        [
          "Raw stdout/stderr",
          "✅ Full",
          "❌ Never"
        ],
        [
          "Source code/diffs",
          "✅ Full",
          "❌ Never"
        ],
        [
          "Secrets/keys",
          "✅ Full",
          "❌ Never"
        ],
        [
          "Action IDs, timestamps",
          "✅ Full",
          "✅ Redacted"
        ],
        [
          "Event counts, statuses",
          "✅ Full",
          "✅ Aggregated"
        ],
        [
          "Hashes (SHA256)",
          "✅ Full",
          "✅ For deduplication"
        ],
        [
          "Ciphertext",
          "✅ Full",
          "✅ If encryption enabled"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "No authoritative receipts in remote audit",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The remote store never holds receipts in a form that could be confused with local authority. Remote event rows are content-light and non-authoritative.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Signed local action envelopes",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Any mutation sent from local cockpit to remote store must be wrapped in a signed local action envelope (see [Local Action Envelope Schema](../schemas/rig.relay.local_action_envelope.v1.schema.json)) containing: - Canonicalized action payload - Replay prevention fields (action_id, nonce, issued_at) - Cryptographic signature (Ed25519)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The remote store verifies the signature against a registered public key before executing any mutation.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Contract Rules",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Backend (local cockpit) is authority. Remote is render-only and append-only. 2. Remote store must not infer governance, checkpointability, or promotion readiness. 3. Missing remote connectivity degrades gracefully to local-only operation. 4. Alpha telemetry is opt-in only. Default is local-first. 5. All remote communication is outbound-initiated. 6. Signed local action envelopes are the only mutation path to remote stores. 7. No raw session tokens, prompts, model outputs, or source code in remote storage.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
